> `jsU_isalpharune`,\n`tolowerrune` -> `jsU_tolowerrune`, `toupperrune` -> `jsU_toupperrune`,\n`islowerrune`/`isupperrune` -> `jsU_islowerrune`/`jsU_isupperrune`. Those are already\nimplemented in src/utf.rs - just call them by their jsU_ names.\n\nOther notes for this file:\n- The C code uses setjmp/longjmp for its own error handling\n  (`struct cstate { jmp_buf kaboom; ... }` and `die()` doing longjmp). Use\n  `crate::jsi::_setjmp` / `crate::jsi::longjmp` with the `jmp_buf` type from jsi\n  (it has exactly the right layout). Put the `jmp_buf` as the first field of the\n  struct exactly like C. Pattern:\n      if _setjmp(std::ptr::addr_of_mut!((*g).kaboom)) != 0 { ...error path... }\n  and `longjmp(std::ptr::addr_of_mut!((*g).kaboom), 1)` in die(). die() returns `!`.\n  IMPORTANT: any local variable of the setjmp-calling function that is written\n  before the longjmp and read in the error path must use `vread`/`vwrite` from jsi\n  (C's `volatile`).\n- The recursive-descent parser uses a global-ish `struct cstate` passed by pointer.\n  Keep the same structure and field names.\n- All the character-class tables, escape handling and the backtracking matcher must\n  be translated literally, including `Rune` (i32) arithmetic and any casts.\n- `struct Resub` is in jsi; `sub[i].sp` / `sub[i].ep` are its fields.\n- If regexp.c declares a `static` variadic function, follow TRANSLATION_GUIDE §5.\n\nWhen done, run:\n  cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-Gclm0f/translated_rust && cargo build --release --message-format=short 2>&1 | grep '^src/regexp.rs'\nand fix every error in YOUR file. Errors of the form \"cannot find function `X`\"\nwhere X is defined in ANOTHER c_src/src/*.c file are expected and must be ignored\n(other modules are still stubs). Repeat until only such errors remain.\n\nReport at the end: the list of functions you translated (marking which are exported),\nand the exact remaining error lines for src/regexp.rs (if any).","uuid":"5bd92044-773